# The build needs pyproject.toml, uv.lock and the source. Everything below is
# either rebuilt in the image, irrelevant to it, or must never enter it.
#
# Docker matches these with filepath.Match, which does NOT recurse on its own --
# `__pycache__/` alone would only match the one at the context root, and every
# nested one would ship the host's bytecode. Hence `**/`.

# A host virtualenv is the wrong platform's binaries; the image builds its own.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Tests and their fixtures are not shipped. `make test` runs on the host, and
# the golden fixture is an oracle for development, not a runtime input. This is
# also why `make eval-router` has no DOCKER=1 mode: its cases live here.
tests/

# Secrets never enter an image (spec 22 §11). The real .env is at the repo root,
# above this build context, so it cannot reach the image in any case; these two
# lines are here so that a stray copy inside backend/ would not change that.
.env
**/.env.*

# Data belongs on a mount, not in a layer: the workbook is the athlete's own
# and is not committed, and the OpenPowerlifting CSV is ~1 GB.
**/*.xlsx
**/*.csv

# Local notes and editor state.
**/*.md
.vscode/
.idea/
